{"user": "i played b6 later thinking it flipped c5 d5 c6 d6 \u2014 it only flipped c5 c6 d6. how do i avoid misreading diagonals like that under time pressure?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:53:55.180606+00:00", "assistant": "Use a quick **8-ray scan** from the square you\u2019re playing.\n\nFor **b6**, check only these straight lines:\n\n- Row: **a6 / c6 d6 e6\u2026**\n- Column: **b5 b4\u2026 / b7 b8**\n- Diagonals: **a5 / c5 d4 e3\u2026** and **a7 / c7 d8**\n\nSo **d5 is not on a diagonal from b6** \u2014 from b6 to d5 is \u201c2 over, 1 up,\u201d like a knight move. Diagonals always change **column and row by 1 each step**.\n\nUnder time pressure, say to yourself:\n\n> \u201cAdjacent enemy? keep going straight. Do I end on my disc? Then flip. If not, no flip.\u201d\n\nAnd in endgames, don\u2019t spend too long counting flips anyway \u2014 first ask: **does this give a corner, lose mobility, or force the last move?**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:53:55.180606+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:54:00.180606+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2, "Solution Request": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 2, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principl